with \code{m} a two-column matrix, or one of the helpers' results:
\code{\link[=lens_polygon]{lens_polygon()}}, \code{\link[=lens_bbox]{lens_bbox()}}, \code{\link[=lens_range]{lens_range()}}, \code{\link[=lens_categories]{lens_categories()}},
\code{\link[=lens_compare]{lens_compare()}}, \code{\link[=lens_cells]{lens_cells()}}, \code{\link[=lens_union]{lens_union()}}.
